      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m just curious what the thinking was here with removing the listener in updateInterfaceState? On one hand, I do agree that there is less code however that comes at the cost of having less useful error messages.\n\nIf removing the listener\u0027s more specific error messaging is the approach landed on, let\u0027s at least update updateInterfaceState to include logs as to why false was returned.\n\neg something like:\n        if (iface \u003d\u003d null) {\n            logw(TAG, \"interface link state is it was already set to \" + up);\n            return false;\n        }\n        \nThis way if there was an expectation that the link state was going to change, if we don\u0027t know why from the listener, at least there will be something explicit in the logs.",
